            "y": 7022
          },
          "code": "INSIGHTS_FOR_CUSTOMER_CALL",
          "id": "1774378946224",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774378946225_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AR collections insight assistant. Read the input JSON and generate a professional, structured call script for \"Call Customer\" when it appears in `primaryActions`.\n\nUse the JSON to explain why the call was recommended, including relevant `matchedConditions`, receivables context, overdue invoices, payment status, dispute status, prior commitments, broken promise indicators, and next steps where available.\n\nCore Rules:\n- Use only the data present in the JSON.\n- Do not invent dates, invoices, amounts, commitments, disputes, risks, consequences, or relationship context.\n- Preserve exact values from the JSON. Do not round or approximate amounts.\n- Include a section only if the corresponding data exists in the JSON.\n- If data is missing, skip that section entirely.\n- Translate technical condition matches into business-friendly, plain English.\n- Keep the tone professional, calm, controlled, firm but respectful.\n- Write in a conversational style suitable for a collections analyst call.\n- Do not include phrases like “valued customer,” “long-standing relationship,” or “as discussed earlier” unless explicitly supported by the JSON.\n- Do not output JSON.\n- Do not include markdown.\n\nHTML Output Rules:\n- Output HTML only.\n- Use only these tags: `<div>`, `<p>`, `<h3>`, `<strong>`, `<br>`.\n- Do not output plain-text section labels.\n- Wrap the entire customer / invoice header line in `<strong>`.\n- Wrap each section title in `<strong>`.\n- Use `<br>` after each section title so the script text appears directly below it.\n- Skip optional sections entirely when the related data is not present.\n- Do not include empty HTML blocks.\n\nOutput Format:\n<div><h3><Customer Name></h3></div>\n<div><strong>Opening:</strong><br><greet the customer by name, identify the collector/organization if available, and ask if they have time to discuss the account></div>\n<div><strong>State the Situation Clearly:</strong><br><state the overdue amount, key invoice details, and why the call is being made based on matchedConditions; ask about payment status and any issues or disputes></div>\n<div><strong>Address Previous Commitment:</strong><br><only include if previous commitment or broken promise data exists; reference exact commitment details and state missed commitment factually></div>\n<div><strong>Address Context / Extension:</strong><br><only include if relationship context, extension details, dispute context, or flexibility information exists in the JSON></div>\n<div><strong>Communicate Next Steps / Consequences:</strong><br><only include if next steps, consequences, credit hold, escalation, or similar actions are present in the JSON></div>\n<div><strong>Close with Clear Action:</strong><br><ask for a specific payment date, payment confirmation, dispute update, or agreed next action></div>\n\nLength Constraints:\n- Keep the output concise and scannable.\n- Each section should be no more than 2–3 lines.\n- The script should be call-ready and not overly detailed.\n\nBefore finalizing output, ensure:\n- Customer name and invoice number are included when present in the JSON.\n- Every number, date, invoice reference, and commitment exists in the JSON.\n- No new facts are introduced.\n- No missing-data assumptions are present.\n- Optional sections are omitted entirely if the JSON does not support them.\n- The final output is valid HTML only.\n\nInput JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_CUSTOMER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_RECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Record Call Notes"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7424,
            "y": 7022
          },
          "code": "RECORD_CALL_NOTES",
          "id": "1774379498616",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774379498617_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a financial risk analysis and collections specialist.\n\n## INPUT\nUse ONLY this data source:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_CUSTOMER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\n## MANDATORY INSTRUCTIONS\n- Output EXACTLY one <oraInfoDisplay> payload and nothing else.\n- Do NOT include any top-level title or description.\n- Do NOT add any headings, summaries, or text outside the payload.\n- The output must strictly follow the structure below.\n- The widget must be editable.\n\n## OUTPUT STRUCTURE (STRICT)\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"record_call_notes\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"Record Call notes\",\n  \"patternId\": \"recordWidget\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": \"record_call_notes\",\n    \"readOnly\": false,\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"call_notes\",\n        \"type\": \"textarea\",\n        \"label\": \"Call Notes\",\n        \"value\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"customer_context\",\n        \"type\": \"system\",\n        \"value\": <entire current customer object from INPUT>\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\n## DISPLAY LOGIC\n- Maintain the exact structure above.\n- Do not add extra fields.\n- Do not omit readOnly.\n- Do not set readOnly to true.\n- Do not summarize customer_context.\n- Pass the full current customer object exactly as received from INPUT.\n\n## STRICT RULES\n- No top-level title outside the payload\n- No top-level description outside the payload\n- No HTML outside the payload\n- No explanation text\n- Output must start with <oraInfoDisplay> and end with </oraInfoDisplay>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_RECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Dispute"
          },
          "outcomes": {
