          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776764523243"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6812,
            "y": 7688
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_PROMISE_DRAFT_CONTENT",
          "id": "1776837446788",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776837446790_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a professional and polite email draft requesting a promise to pay from a customer with multiple overdue invoices.  \n\n---\n\n### Context:\n- Overdue Balance = Only the portion of the outstanding balance that is past due.\n- Outstanding Balance = All unpaid/open invoices, regardless of due date.\n- Customer Name: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.CustomerName}}  \n- Overdue Amount: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.TotalOverdueAmount}}  \n- Overdue Invoice Count: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.OverdueInvoiceCount}}  \n- Overdue Invoice List : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.OverdueInvoices}} invoice_list with transactionNumber, transactionDate, installmentDueDate, amountRemaining, daysOverdue\n- Collector Name: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.CollectorName}}\n\n---\n\n### Instructions:\n- Address it without customer name\n- Treat the Overdue Invoice List as already ordered by Overdue Amount\n- Present the first 10 invoices in a clean table format (Invoice Number, Invoice Date, Due Date, Amount Remaining, Days Overdue) using an HTML table only with visible borders.\n- The invoice table must use only these table tags: <table>, <thead>, <tbody>, <tr>, <th>, <td>\n- Do not use markdown tables, pipe characters, dashed table separators, or plain text table formatting.\n- If fewer than 10 invoices exist, include all invoices  \n- If the overdue invoices contain more than one currencyCode, add a \"Currency\" column to the invoice table and display currencyCode. If all invoices are in the same currency, omit the Currency column and display amounts in that single currency. When presenting the total overdue amount, group and display totals by currency using the TotalOverdueAmount structure ({ totalOverdueAmount,currencyCode}) instead of combining different currencies into a single total.\n- Format currency and dates consistently  \n- Maintain a polite, professional, and non-aggressive tone  \n- Include a clear request for a specific promise-to-pay date  \n- Offer assistance in case of disputes or issues  \n- Keep the email concise and easy to read  \n- Email signature with Collector Name(only if present or keep it empty), Customer Account Specialist –  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.CustomerName}}\n---\n\n### Output Format:\nStructured email body with:\n- Context of Overdue Amount, Overdue Invoice Count\n- Table of top 10 overdue invoices\n- Clear call-to-action (request for payment date)  \n- Polite closing\n\n\n## Output Specification\n{ \"content\": \"generated email body content\" }\n\n## CRITICAL OUTPUT RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n- Output must be plain text only\n- DO NOT use Markdown symbols (###, **, _, #)\n- Use ONLY:\n  - Plain text\n  - Hyphen (-) bullets\n  - Line breaks\n  - HTML tags (ONLY the allowed tags are <h1>, <h2>, <h3>, <h4>, <h5>, <h6>, <span>, <strong>, <br/>)\n- DO NOT combine sections into paragraphs\n- DO NOT generate a “Summary” section or sentence\n- DO NOT add “Generated using …” text\n- Follow the exact section order STRICTLY"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776837446788_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"content\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Professional and polite promise-to-pay email body generated from the provided customer overdue invoice data\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"content\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
