            "y": 7910
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_PROMISE_TO_PAY_DRAFT_REVIEW",
          "id": "1776764523243",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776764523243_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Objective1\nGenerate a concise (max 3 sentences) justification for recommending “Request Promise-to-Pay”, using only the most decision-relevant data.\n\n---\n\n### Inputs\n- Customer Name: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.CustomerName}}    \n- Total Outstanding: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.TotalOutstandingAmount}} \n- Total Overdue: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.TotalOverdueAmount}}    \n- Overdue %: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.TotalOverdueAmount}}/{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.TotalOutstandingAmount}}  (must be calculated if not provided)  \n- Overdue Invoice Count: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.OverdueInvoiceCount}}  \n- Overdue Invoice List: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.OverdueInvoices}} invoice_list with invoice_number, invoice_date, due_date, open amount, days_overdue  \n\n---\n\n### Instructions\n\n#### 1. Core Logic (MANDATORY)\n- Justification MUST be driven by:  \n  - Overdue magnitude (amount + %)  \n  - Aging severity (max days or highest bucket)  \n  - Exposure scale (invoice count)  \n  - Risk level  \n- Combine at least 2–3 signals, not just one  \n\n#### 2. Output Rules\n- Maximum 3 sentences  \n- No repetition of all inputs—only key drivers  \n- No generic phrases (e.g., “timely follow-up needed”)  \n- Do NOT mention SOP/rules explicitly  \n- Avoid overly technical jargon—keep it business-friendly and actionable  \n\n#### 3. Mandatory Ending\n- Always append:  \n  A draft email to request a Promise-to-Pay has been prepared for your review.  \n\n#### 4. Tone\n- Neutral, informative, and professional  \n- Do not sound accusatory or customer-facing (this is internal-facing)  \n\n---\n\n### Output Format\n\n{{2-sentence justification}}  \n\n---\n\n### Example Output\n\n**Why this action is recommended**  \nThis account has a high overdue exposure (62% of total balance) with invoices aging beyond 30 days and an oldest delinquency of 45 days, indicating increasing payment risk. Securing a Promise-to-Pay will help establish a firm repayment timeline— a draft email is ready for your review.\n\n### Objective2\n\nYou are provided with promise-to-pay email data below:\n`{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result}}`\n\nProduce one `email` communication suggestion labelled `Review and Send Email` in the following exact `oraComms` structure:\n\n```xml\n<oraComms>\n{\n  \"title\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.title}}\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.description}}\",\n  \"content\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_PROMISE_DRAFT_CONTENT.$output.content}}\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Send Email\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"targetAgent\": \"ORA_FIN_IEX_COLLECTIONS_ACTION_ASSISTANT\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"Recipient\",\n      \"description\": \"Email address of the recipients. If there are multiple recipients, provide them as comma-separated values.\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.to}}\",\n      \"editable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc\",\n      \"title\": \"cc\",\n      \"description\": \"CC email address of the recipients. If there are multiple recipients, provide them as comma-separated values.\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.cc}}\",\n      \"editable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Subject\",\n      \"description\": \"Subject line for the email.\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.subject}}\",\n      \"editable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"accountNumber\",\n      \"title\": \"Account Number\",\n      \"description\": \"Customer account number.\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.AccountNumber}}\",\n      \"editable\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"partyNumber\",\n      \"title\": \"Party Number\",\n      \"description\": \"Customer party number.\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.PartyNumber}}\",\n      \"editable\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</oraComms>\nImportant content rules:\n- Do not display any extra field called `email content` outside the `oraComms` params structure\n- Do not print the email body separately outside `oraComms`\n- Do not print the subject separately outside `oraComms`\n- Print the email communication button as `Review and Send`\n- actionText must be \"Send Email\"\n- Always position email communication option above low priority action\n\nGenerate a low priority action labeled `Skip` Use this exact `followUpCommand` value for the action:\n- `ora.Agent(oraSkipSendingPromiseReminder,{\"accountNumber\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.AccountNumber}}\",\"partyNumber\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.PartyNumber}}\",\"customerAccountId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_INSTALLMENTS_REQUIRING_PROMISE.$output.result.CustomerAccountId}}\"})`\n\n## Critical Output Rules\n- Output must be plain text only\n- Do not use Markdown symbols (`###`, `**`, `_`, `#`) in the generated final output\n\n- Use only:\n  - Plain text\n  - Hyphen (`-`) bullets\n  - Line breaks\n  - HTML tags only from this allowed set:\n    - `<h1>`\n    - `<h2>`\n    - `<h3>`\n    - `<h4>`\n    - `<h5>`\n    - `<h6>`\n    - `<span>`\n    - `<strong>`\n    - `<br/>`\n- Do not combine sections into paragraphs\n- Do not generate a `Summary` section or sentence\n- Do not add `Generated using ...` text\n- Follow the exact section order strictly\n\n## Strict Validation\n\n- Do not generate any summary text outside the cardWidget\n- Do not generate any numbered actions in content\n- Do not generate any resolution or conclusion statements\n- Do not duplicate the subject\n- Do not duplicate the email content\n\nIf any of the above validation rules fail, rewrite the output until it passes."
            },
            {
              "id": "1776764523243_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Processing promise detail information from email message",
            "name": "Process Email Message Details for Promises",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let sourceOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_REFERENCE_FORMAT_DATA_FOR_PROMISES.$output;\nlet result = sourceOutput.result !== undefined ? sourceOutput.result : sourceOutput;\n\nif (typeof result === \"string\") {\n  result = JSON.parse(result);\n}\n\nif (typeof result === \"string\") {\n  result = JSON.parse(result);\n}\n\nreturn result;",
            "errorNodeId": "1778436031247"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778489311691"
          },
