          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_DISPUTE_DETAILS_FOR_EMAIL",
          "id": "1778177206880",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778177206880_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1778177206880_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate `<oraInfoDisplay>` as a multiRecordWidget for dispute details using only this upstream JSON as the source of truth:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result}}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Return only valid output. Do not include markdown, explanations, comments, or code fences.\n1a. All generated summary or guidance text must appear only inside the `description` field of the `<oraInfoDisplay>` JSON. Do not print `description`, summary text, guidance text, or any other text outside `<oraInfoDisplay>` or `<oraInsight>` blocks. Always title and description should be displayed above the table.\n2. Read all values directly from the upstream JSON. Do not invent, infer, or hardcode row data.\n3. First construct the `oraInfoDisplay` with key using the root-level intentCode and messageId in this shape:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"<intentCode-messageId >\">\n   {\n     \"title\": \"Dispute Details\",\n     \"description\": \"<summary from upstream json with additional status-based guidance appended when applicable>\",\n     \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n     \"properties\": {\n       \"cols\": [...],\n       \"rows\": [...]\n     }\n   }\n   </oraInfoDisplay>\n4. Set `title` exactly to `Dispute Details`.\n5. Set `description` using the root-level `summary` field from the upstream JSON as the base value. If `summary` is missing, null, or empty, use an empty string as the base value. Preserve transaction details such as `TransactionNumber` exactly as provided in the upstream JSON.\n6. Append additional text to `description` based on root `status` as follows:\n   - If root `status` is `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, do not append any extra text.\n   - If root `status` is `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`, append this guidance to the base summary: ` Create valid disputes and manually review and process the error ones.`\n   - If root `status` is `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, append this guidance to the base summary: ` Review the error ones and manually process them.`\n7. Set `patternId` exactly to `multiRecordWidget`.\n8. Read these root-level fields from the upstream JSON:\n   - `status`\n   - `summary`\n   - `items`\n   - `messageId`\n   - `intentCode`\n9. Treat `items` as the row source. If `items` is missing or not an array, use an empty array.\n9a. If `items` is missing, null, not an array, or an empty array, return only this `oraInfoDisplay` and do not generate any `oraInsight`:\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"<intentCode-messageId >\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"Dispute Details\",\n  \"description\": \"No Records Found\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [],\n    \"rows\": []\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n10. Always include these columns in this exact order:\n   - Transaction Number\n   - Transaction Date\n   - Amount Remaining\n   - Currency\n   - Due Date\n   - Dispute Amount\n   - Dispute Section\n   - Dispute Reason\n   - Customer Comments\n11. Add these extra columns only when root `status` is either `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` or `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`:\n   - Status\n   - Error Details\n12. For each row, map values from each item in this exact order:\n   - `TransactionNumber`\n   - `TransactionDate`\n   - `TransactionAmountRemaining`\n   - `TransactionCurrency`\n   - `DueDate`\n   - `DisputeAmount`\n   - `DisputeSection`\n   - `DisputeReason`\n   - `CustomerComments`\n13. Preserve `TransactionNumber` exactly as provided in the upstream JSON.\n   - Do not remove underscores, spaces, hyphens, leading zeroes, or any other characters.\n   - Do not normalize, trim, reformat, parse, cast, or transform it in any way.\n   - Always display it exactly as received from the source item.\n   - Use empty string for any missing scalar field values.\n14. For `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, show only the base columns.\n15. For `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` and `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, show the base columns plus `Status` and `Error Details`.\n16. For review rows, derive the `Status` cell as a badge object:\n   - If `ProcessingStatusCode` is `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` or `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, use:\n     {\n       \"type\": \"badge\",\n       \"text\": \"VALID\",\n       \"priority\": \"success\"\n     }\n   - Otherwise use:\n     {\n       \"type\": \"badge\",\n       \"text\": \"INVALID\",\n       \"priority\": \"alert\"\n     }\n17. `priority` values must only use supported values. In this case use only `success` or `alert`.\n18. For review rows, derive `Error Details` from `ErrorDetails`:\n   - If `ErrorDetails` is not an array or is empty, use an empty string\n   - If it is an array, collect each element’s `errorText`; if `errorText` is missing, use `message`; skip blanks; join all messages with `; `\n19. Each row must be returned as:\n   {\n     \"cells\": [ ... ]\n   }\n20. After the closing `</oraInfoDisplay>` tag, generate each low priority action as a separate wrapped `<oraInsight>` block only when `items` exists as a non-empty array. Do not output raw JSON outside an `<oraInsight>` wrapper. Do not print any text between `</oraInfoDisplay>` and `<oraInsight>`.\n21. Generate one separate `<oraInsight>` block per low priority action.\n22. For root `status` = `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, generate two low priority `oraInsight` actions:\n   - `Create Dispute`\n   - `Manual Review`\n23. For root `status` = `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`, generate two low priority `oraInsight` actions:\n   - `Create Valid Dispute`\n   - `Manual Review`\n24. For root `status` = `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, generate one low priority `oraInsight` action:\n   - `Manual Review`\n25. Use these exact followUpCommand values for the separate `oraInsight` actions:\n   - For `Create Dispute`:\n     `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"process\"})`\n   - For `Create Valid Dispute`:\n     `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"process\"})`\n   - For `Manual Review`:\n     `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_DISPUTES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"skip\"})`\n26. The logic must correctly handle all of these root `status` values:\n   - `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`\n   - `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`\n   - `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Construct actionable payload for disputes",
            "name": "Construct Actionable Payload For Disputes",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/* source actionable detail records */\nlet inputData = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_BO_GET_ACTIONABLE_DETAILS_FROM_EMAIL_MESSAGE.$output;\nlet records = Array.isArray(inputData) ? inputData : [];\n\n/* source lookup BO outputs */\nlet disputeSectionsOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_BO_GET_DISPUTE_SECTIONS.$output;\nlet disputeReasonsOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_BO_GET_DISPUTE_REASON.$output;\nlet disputeTypesOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_BO_GET_DISPUTE_TYPE.$output;\n\nlet disputeSections = Array.isArray(disputeSectionsOutput) ? disputeSectionsOutput : [];\nlet disputeReasons = Array.isArray(disputeReasonsOutput) ? disputeReasonsOutput : [];\nlet disputeTypes = Array.isArray(disputeTypesOutput) ? disputeTypesOutput : [];\n\nfunction buildLookupMap(items, codeKey, meaningKey) {\n  let map = {};\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n    let item = items[i] || {};\n    let code = item[codeKey];\n    let meaning = item[meaningKey];\n\n    if (code !== undefined && code !== null && code !== \"\") {\n      map[String(code)] = meaning !== undefined && meaning !== null ? meaning : \"\";\n    }\n  }\n\n  return map;\n}\n\nlet disputeSectionMap = buildLookupMap(disputeSections, \"DISPUTESECTIONCODE\", \"DISPUTESECTION\");\nlet disputeReasonMap = buildLookupMap(disputeReasons, \"DISPUTEREASONCODE\", \"DISPUTEREASON\");\nlet disputeTypeMap = buildLookupMap(disputeTypes, \"DISPUTETYPECODE\", \"DISPUTETYPE\");\n\nfunction parseRequestData(requestData) {\n  if (typeof requestData === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(requestData);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return {};\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (requestData && typeof requestData === \"object\") {\n    return requestData;\n  }\n\n  return {};\n}\n\nfunction resolveMeaning(code, lookupMap) {\n  if (code === undefined || code === null || code === \"\") {\n    return code;\n  }\n\n  let codeText = String(code);\n  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(lookupMap, codeText)) {\n    return lookupMap[codeText];\n  }\n\n  return code;\n}\n\n/* construct request payload list */\nlet output = records.map((item) => {\n  let requestData = parseRequestData(item && item.REQUESTDATA ? item.REQUESTDATA : null);\n  let payload = requestData && requestData.actionablePayload ? requestData.actionablePayload : null;\n\n  if (payload && typeof payload === \"object\") {\n    payload.DisputeReason = resolveMeaning(payload.DisputeReason, disputeReasonMap);\n    payload.DisputeSection = resolveMeaning(payload.DisputeSection, disputeSectionMap);\n    payload.DisputeType = resolveMeaning(payload.DisputeType, disputeTypeMap);\n  }\n\n  return {\n    id: item && item.CUSTOMERMESSAGEDETAILID !== undefined ? item.CUSTOMERMESSAGEDETAILID : null,\n    path: \"/receivablesDisputes\",\n    operation: \"create\",\n    payload: payload\n  };\n});\n\n/* final result */\nlet result = output;\nreturn result;",
            "errorNodeId": "1778436031247"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776682439797"
          },
