          "id": "1778489311691",
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_PROMISE_TO_PAY_DETAILS_FOR_EMAIL",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778489311691_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Prompt Reference of promise-to-Pay:\n\nGenerate `oraInfoDisplay` as a multiRecordWidget for promise-to-Pay details using only this upstream JSON as the source of truth:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result}}\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Return only valid output. Do not include markdown, explanations, comments, or code fences.\n1a. All generated summary or guidance text must appear only inside the `description` field of the `<oraInfoDisplay>` JSON. Do not print `description`, summary text, guidance text, or any other text outside `<oraInfoDisplay>` or `<oraInsight>` blocks. Always title and description should be displayed above the table.\n2. Read all values directly from the upstream JSON. Do not invent, infer, or hardcode row data.\n3. First construct the `oraInfoDisplay` with key using the root-level intentCode and messageId in this shape:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"<intentCode-messageId >\">\n   {\n   \"title\": \"Promise to Pay Details\",\n   \"description\": \"<summary from upstream json with additional status-based guidance appended when applicable>\",\n   \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n   \"properties\": {\n   \"cols\": [...],\n   \"rows\": [...]\n   }\n   } </oraInfoDisplay>\n4. Set `title` exactly to `Promise to Pay Details`.\n5. Set `description` using the root-level `summary.summaryText` field from the upstream JSON as the base value. If `summary.summaryText` is missing, null, or empty, use an empty string as the base value.\n6. Append additional text to `description` based on root `status` as follows:\n\n   * If root `status` is `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, do not append any extra text.\n   * If root `status` is `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`, append this guidance to the base summary: ` Create only valid promises and manually review the error ones.`\n   * If root `status` is `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, append this guidance to the base summary: ` Review the error ones and manually process them.`\n7. Set `patternId` exactly to `multiRecordWidget`.\n8. Read these root-level fields from the upstream JSON:\n\n   * `status`\n   * `summary`\n   * `items`\n   * `errors`\n   * `messageId`\n   * `intentCode`\n9. Treat `items` as the row source. If `items` is missing or not an array, use an empty array.\n9a. If `items` is missing, null, not an array, or an empty array, return only this `oraInfoDisplay` and do not generate any `oraInsight`:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"<intentCode-messageId >\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"Promise to Pay Details\",\n  \"description\": \"No Records Found\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [],\n    \"rows\": []\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n10. Always include these columns in this exact order:\n\n* Invoice Number\n* Invoice Date\n* Due Date\n* Amount Remaining\n* Currency\n* Promise Amount\n* Promise Date\n\n11. Add these extra columns only when root `status` is either `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` or `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`:\n\n* Status\n* Error Details\n\n12. For each row, map values from each item in this exact order:\n\n* `TransactionNumber`\n* `TransactionDate`\n* `InstallmentDueDate`\n* `TransactionAmountRemaining`\n* `TransactionCurrency`\n* `PromiseAmount`\n* `PromiseDate`\n\n13. Preserve `TransactionNumber` exactly as provided in the upstream JSON.\n\n* Do not remove underscores, spaces, hyphens, leading zeroes, or any other characters.\n* Do not normalize, trim, reformat, parse, cast, or transform it in any way.\n* Always display it exactly as received from the source item.\n* Use empty string for any missing scalar field values.\n\n14. For `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, show only the base columns.\n15. For `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` and `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, show the base columns plus `Status` and `Error Details`.\n16. For review rows, derive the `Status` cell as a badge object:\n\n* If `ProcessingStatusCode` is `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` or `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, use:\n  {\n  \"type\": \"badge\",\n  \"text\": \"VALID\",\n  \"priority\": \"success\"\n  }\n* Otherwise use:\n  {\n  \"type\": \"badge\",\n  \"text\": \"INVALID\",\n  \"priority\": \"alert\"\n  }\n\n17. `priority` values must only use supported values. In this case use only `success` or `alert`.\n18. For review rows, derive `Error Details` from `ErrorDetails`:\n\n* If `ErrorDetails` is not an array or is empty, use an empty string\n* If it is an array, collect each element’s `errorText`; if `errorText` is missing, use `message`; skip blanks; join all messages with `; `\n\n19. Each row must be returned as:\n    {\n    \"cells\": [ ... ]\n    }\n20. After `oraInfoDisplay`, generate separate `oraInsight` entries for low priority actions. Do not include low priority actions inside `oraInfoDisplay` JSON.\n21. Generate one separate `<oraInsight>` block per low priority action.\n22. For root `status` = `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`, generate two low priority `oraInsight` actions:\n\n* `Create Promise to Pay`\n* `Manual Review`\n\n23. For root `status` = `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`, generate two low priority `oraInsight` actions:\n\n* `Create Only Valid Promises`\n* `Manual Review`\n\n24. For root `status` = `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, generate one low priority `oraInsight` action:\n\n* `Manual Review`\n\n25. Use these exact followUpCommand values for the separate `oraInsight` actions:\n\n* For `Create Promise to Pay`:\n  `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"process\"})`\n* For `Create Only Valid Promises`:\n  `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"process\"})`\n* For `Manual Review`:\n  `ora.Agent(emailActions,{\"action\":\"emailActions\",\"messageId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.messageId}}\",\"intentCode\":\"{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_PROCESS_EMAIL_MESSAGE_DETAILS_FOR_PROMISES.$output.result.intentCode}}\",\"actionType\":\"skip\"})`\n\n26. The logic must correctly handle all of these root `status` values:\n\n* `ORA_ACTION_PENDING`\n* `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`\n* `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Constructing payload for getting message details for PO update",
            "name": "Construct Payload for Getting Message Details for PO Update",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let pMessageId = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CUSTOMER_DETAILS.$output.result.messageId;\nlet pIntentCode = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CUSTOMER_DETAILS.$output.result.intentCode;\n\nlet requestPayload = {\n  parameters: {\n    bindMessageId: pMessageId,\n    bindIntentCode: pIntentCode\n  },\n  viewQueries: {\n    collectionsCustomerMessageDetails: {\n      view: \"collectionsCustomerMessageDetails\",\n      businessObject: \"CollectionsCustomerMessage\",\n      module: \"oraErpCoreAdvancedCollections\",\n      fieldAliases: {\n        \"customerMessageDetailId\": \"customerMessageDetailId\",\n        \"emailMessage.messageId\": \"messageId\",\n        \"customerTransaction.customerTransactionId\": \"customerTransactionId\",\n        \"processingStatus.lookupCode\": \"processingStatusCode\",\n        \"intent.lookupCode\": \"intentCode\",\n        \"requestData\": \"requestData\",\n        \"responseData\": \"responseData\",\n        \"accountSitePurpose.siteUseId\": \"siteUseId\",\n        \"customerAccount.customerAccountId\": \"accountId\",\n        \"customer.id\": \"partyId\"\n      }\n    },\n    receivablesPaymentSchedules: {\n      module: \"oraErpCoreReceivablesBilling\",\n      businessObject: \"ReceivablesTransactionPaymentSchedule\",\n      view: \"receivablesPaymentSchedule\",\n      fieldAliases: {\n        \"transactionDate\": \"transactionDate\",\n        \"amountRemaining\": \"amountRemaining\",\n        \"transactionNumber\": \"transactionNumber\",\n        \"invoiceCurrency.currencyCode\": \"currencyCode\",\n        \"customerAccount.accountNumber\": \"accountNumber\",\n        \"customerAccount.customer.name\": \"partyName\",\n        \"customerTransaction.customerTransactionId\": \"customerTransactionId\",\n        \"installmentDueDate\": \"dueDate\",\n        \"customerTransaction.batchSource.name\": \"customerTransactionSource\",\n        \"customerTransaction.customerTransactionType.name\": \"customerTransactionType\",\n        \"customerTransaction.businessUnit.name\": \"businessUnit\",\n        \"customerTransaction.pONumber\": \"currentPONumber\",\n        \"customerTransaction.pODate\": \"currentPODate\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  select: \"select cmd.customerMessageDetailId customerMessageDetailId, cmd.messageId messageId, cmd.customerTransactionId customerTransactionId, cmd.processingStatusCode processingStatusCode, cmd.intentCode intentCode, cmd.requestData requestData, cmd.responseData responseData, cmd.siteUseId siteUseId, cmd.accountId accountId, cmd.partyId partyId, rps.transactionNumber transactionNumber, to_char(rps.transactionDate,'YYYY-MM-DD') transactionDate, to_char(rps.dueDate,'YYYY-MM-DD') dueDate, rps.amountRemaining amountRemaining, rps.currencyCode currencyCode, rps.accountNumber accountNumber, rps.partyName partyName, rps.customerTransactionSource customerTransactionSource, rps.customerTransactionType customerTransactionType, rps.businessUnit businessUnit, rps.currentPONumber currentPONumber, to_char(rps.currentPODate,'YYYY-MM-DD') currentPODate from collectionsCustomerMessageDetails cmd, (select receivablesPaymentSchedules.customerTransactionId customerTransactionId, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.transactionNumber) transactionNumber, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.transactionDate) transactionDate, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.dueDate) dueDate, sum(receivablesPaymentSchedules.amountRemaining) amountRemaining, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.currencyCode) currencyCode, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.accountNumber) accountNumber, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.partyName) partyName, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.customerTransactionSource) customerTransactionSource, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.customerTransactionType) customerTransactionType, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.businessUnit) businessUnit, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.currentPONumber) currentPONumber, max(receivablesPaymentSchedules.currentPODate) currentPODate from receivablesPaymentSchedules group by receivablesPaymentSchedules.customerTransactionId) rps where cmd.intentCode = :bindIntentCode and cmd.messageId = :bindMessageId and cmd.customerTransactionId = rps.customerTransactionId\"\n};\n\nlet result = requestPayload;\nreturn result;"
          },
